# Normalize text files to LF in the index AND in the working tree.
#
# The index is already LF everywhere (`git ls-files --eol` → `i/lf` for every
# tracked text file), but `core.autocrlf=true` checks a Windows working tree out
# as CRLF. Prettier compares against the file on disk, so without `eol=lf` a
# fresh clone on Windows would fail `npm run format:check` on line endings alone,
# in files nobody had touched. This pins the two tools to the same answer.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, so git never tries to normalize or diff them as text.
*.ttf binary
*.woff2 binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary

# Keep the patch-package diffs byte-exact: they are applied by line, and a
# line-ending rewrite makes `patch-package` fail to apply them at all.
patches/** -text
